# End-to-end QEMU coverage of an appliance that starts with MPLS in use
# (spec-kernel-capability-gate AC-15).
#
# Drives internal/le/test/qemu/mplsboot.go, which builds a HOST ze, inits an
# appliance whose seed configuration is gokrazy/ze/ze.conf plus `set fib kernel`
# and `set ldp`, builds the gokrazy image, boots it in QEMU, and asks the Ze CLI
# `show ldp neighbor | json` over SSH. That configuration puts MPLS in use, so
# the kernel capability gate refuses to start Ze on a kernel without MPLS
# routing, and a refused daemon has no SSH server to answer. Only the LDP engine
# answers the question, so the answer also proves the gate judged the MPLS
# configuration rather than a default one.
#
# The driver self-skips like vpp-hugepages-qemu.ci: no QEMU, sshpass, e2fsprogs
# or go toolchain is a SKIP, and an appliance that never answers is a SKIP only
# under software emulation. Under kvm or hvf it is a FAIL. Both PASS and SKIP
# exit 0. The exhaustive run is `./le test qemu mpls-boot-test`.

# The derived timeout would settle on the seconds a SKIP takes. A host ze build,
# an appliance init, a gokrazy image build and a QEMU boot need far more, so the
# budget is pinned to the real cost, as vpp-hugepages-qemu.ci does.
option=timeout:value=900s
cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=./le test qemu mpls-boot-test
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:pattern=APPLIANCE-MPLS-QEMU: (PASS|SKIP)
